A||||2||SCCA FIERO||I FOUND THE ONE
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||06-05-99||01:58 AM||||I have wanted an 88 model for some time now. About a month ago I almost bought a hammered, tired, faded, auto 88 coupe. The other day I saw a red, shiny, 5 speed coupe sitting in the back of a new car dealer. I stopped and looked at it and saw it had "$2,250" on the windsheild. I started it up and it purred like a kitten. The 5 speed box was slick too. It did have "hot" A/C and rear defogger but not much else. 109,000 on the odometer and worn tires. I figured the A/C could be fixed and i have extra tires. I drove it and noticed a banging noise at the right front wheel. I couldn't figure it out and almost left. I finally found the problem. The swaybar link was busted at the top(no bushings) so the link was hitting the swaybar. A 10 dollar fix. This car is solid and tight. It handles better that my 86 even with a busted swaybar. I bought it for $1,700(including taxes) a bargain i think. The brakes are firm and solid. They stop the car faster than my 86 could any day and the Lotus suspension keeps the front from diving into the ground.(My 86 would nose-dive pretty bad)I wanted an 88 for autoxing and although it's underpowered i think my times will improve. I will see on Sunday...
Z||000001||Patrick||06-05-99||02:05 AM||||<br>Sounds like a <b>great</b> deal...<p>I'm jealous.  <IMG SRC="http://forums.gagames.com/forums/frown.gif"> <p><p>
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||06-12-99||11:05 PM||||Today I got a set of 87GT wheels. I went and got some black paint and painted the inside black just like the Formulas have. I'm on my way to building a Formula just better on a budget. The wheels were given to me and have almost new tires on them. Soon the V6 goes in and the spoiler from the same donor car goes on. I still haven't decided if I will add my power windows and locks. Would it be hard? The project car (an 88 coupe) doesn't have them.
